     "level": "I",
     "q": "How do IN and EXISTS subqueries differ?",
     "a": "`IN (subquery)` compares a value with the set the subquery returns. `EXISTS (subquery)` is true if the subquery returns at least one row, and is usually correlated to the outer row.",
     "e": "Modern optimisers often run both the same way. The real difference is NULL handling with `NOT IN`.",
     "code": "SELECT name FROM products\nWHERE id IN (SELECT product_id FROM order_items WHERE quantity >= 5);\nSELECT name FROM products p\nWHERE EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM order_items oi WHERE oi.product_id = p.id AND oi.quantity >= 5);",
