     "level": "A",
     "q": "What is a correlated subquery?",
     "a": "A subquery that references columns from the outer query, so it's logically evaluated once per outer row. For example, \"employees earning more than their department's average\".",
     "e": "They're clear but can be slow on large tables; rewriting with a join to an aggregated subquery or a window function is often faster.",
     "code": "SELECT e.name, e.salary, e.dept_id\nFROM employees e\nWHERE e.salary > (SELECT AVG(salary) FROM employees x WHERE x.dept_id = e.dept_id)\nORDER BY e.dept_id;",
