     "level": "I",
     "q": "What is a CTE (WITH clause)?",
     "a": "A Common Table Expression: a named temporary result defined with `WITH name AS (...)` that the main query can use like a table. You can chain several CTEs.",
     "e": "CTEs make complex queries readable step by step, like variables in code.",
     "code": "WITH revenue AS (\n  SELECT order_id, SUM(quantity * unit_price) AS total FROM order_items GROUP BY order_id\n)\nSELECT o.customer_id, SUM(r.total) AS spent\nFROM orders o JOIN revenue r ON r.order_id = o.id\nGROUP BY o.customer_id ORDER BY spent DESC LIMIT 3;",
