     "level": "I",
     "q": "What do LAG and LEAD do?",
     "a": "`LAG(col, n)` returns the value from n rows before the current row in the window order; `LEAD(col, n)` returns the value n rows after. The optional third argument is the default when there's no such row.",
     "e": "They're perfect for period-over-period comparisons (this month vs last month) and gaps between events.",
