     "q": "What is an UPSERT?",
     "a": "Insert a row, or update it if it already exists (a key conflict). SQLite and PostgreSQL use `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (key) DO UPDATE SET ...`; MySQL uses `ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE`; SQL Server, Oracle and Snowflake use `MERGE`.",
     "e": "`excluded.col` refers to the value you tried to insert.",
