     "level": "I",
     "q": "Surrogate key vs natural key: which should you use?",
     "a": "A natural key has business meaning (email, PAN, ISBN); a surrogate key is a meaningless generated id. Surrogates are stable, compact and never change, so they're the usual primary key; still add a UNIQUE constraint on the natural key.",
     "e": "Emails change and \"unique\" business codes get reused, which is exactly why surrogates win.",
