     "level": "I",
     "q": "How do you compare NULLs safely?",
     "a": "`a = b` is unknown when either side is NULL. Use `a IS NOT DISTINCT FROM b` (standard, PostgreSQL, Snowflake), `a IS b` (SQLite) or `a <=> b` (MySQL), which treat two NULLs as equal.",
